            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery ectasia in a patient with myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>36-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">CVJ-21.019</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a case of triple-vessel coronary artery ectasia (CAE) in a young patient. This patient presented with anterior wall myocardial infarction (MI) with post-infarct angina. His coronary angiogram revealed coronary artery ectasia involving the left anterior descending, circumflex and right coronary arteries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
